site_memo:
This prospective cohort study was performed as part of the ongoing China National Birth Cohort Study from 
March 2017 to May 2020. The study design was approved by the Ethics Committee of the International Peace Maternity and Child Health Hospital (affiliated with the Shanghai Jiao Tong University School of Medicine; 
approval no.: GKLW2016-21).

exclusion_criteria:
We excluded women with pre-pregnancy hypertension, and restricted our cohort to nulliparous women, as pre-eclampsia status in a woman's first pregnancy strongly predicts her risks of pre-eclampsia in subsequent pregnancies19. We excluded pregnancies of women without early pregnancy body mass index (BMI; kg/m2
) or no gestational weight gain measurement and cases of pre-eclampsia where the date of diagnosis
was unknown.

exposure_group_notes:
High BMI = overweight (BMI 24-27.9 kg/m2
), or obese (BMI ≥ 28 kg/m2)
Low BMI = normal weight (BMI 18.5-23.9 kg/m2)

